// Executables already run their top-level statements as a cooperative
// root task. `run` remains available for an explicit nested scheduler
// scope; it uses the same core task effects and scheduler.

// Runs `root_task` and every task it spawns in a nested cooperative scope.
//
// The scheduler intercepts `yield`, channel waits, timers, and nested spawns;
// ordinary host effects continue to the enclosing program fallbacks. It returns
// only after the complete spawned task tree finishes. If every task is blocked,
// the worker parks until a registered channel or timer can make progress.
pub func run(consume root_task: Task) -> () {
	_run_cooperative(root_task: root_task)
}
